<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Snettisham Hoard</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Snettisham Hoard is a series of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> treasure deposits found at Snettisham in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norfolk">Norfolk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, from 1948 onwards. It includes many gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> torcs, among them the Great Torc, buried in the 1st century BCE, together with coins and ingots. Most of it is in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-museum">British Museum</a>, and it is associated with the Iceni.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/snettisham-hoard.jpg" alt="Snettisham Hoard" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Portable Antiquities Scheme from London, England · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Snettisham_Hoard.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
